UX-028 (expand export dialog options) is implemented on branch
feat/UX-028-export-dialog-options — check `gh pr list` before assuming it's
merged.

What it changed, and what's worth knowing before touching exports again:
- Every single-page export (PNG/JPEG/PDF/SVG) now crops to one ExportBounds
  from exportBounds() in exporters.ts — the full artboard, or the selection's
  box (plus its effect clones) clipped to the artboard. Rasters crop via
  toDataURL/toCanvasElement left/top/width/height, the PDF page is sized to
  it, SVG crops with the viewBox. All in untransformed artboard coordinates.
- Selection-only exports hide everything else for the duration of the render
  (withOnlySelection), including a group's other children during in-place
  group editing. For SVG this has to stub each dropped object's own toSVG:
  fabric's Group serializes every child regardless of excludeFromExport, a
  hidden one just gets `visibility: hidden`. exporters.fabric.test.ts pins
  that against real fabric (node-canvas).
- PNG's "Transparent background" toggle defaults ON, per the ticket: the
  background colour goes to '' and the background image is dropped for the
  export. Off flattens onto the background colour, or white. A behaviour
  change from the old as-is PNG — revisit the default if users trip on it.
- Exporters now take an options object, not positional scale/quality/cutLines.
  slugify is gone; sanitizeFileName keeps the user's case and spaces, and the
  book PDF uses it too ("My Book.pdf", no longer "my-book.pdf").
- A selection export carries no product cut line — that's a print-file thing.

